15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting patient selection for a study on DFSP, starting with 1,409 cases, followed by sequential exclusions based on recurrence, prior treatment, lack of ultrasound assessment, age below eighteen, or lesion size over eleven centimeters, yielding 220 patients for analysis divided into HFUS-only and HFUS+CEUS groups, with additional breakdown for propensity score matching.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a close-up photograph of skin with purple surgical markings outlining a mass. Panel B presents a grayscale ultrasound image depicting an oval-shaped lesion. Panel C displays color Doppler ultrasound with red and blue flow signals around and within the lesion. Panel D provides another Doppler ultrasound showing a blood vessel adjacent to the mass. Panel E contains a gross pathology specimen with a large cystic structure surrounded by fatty tissue, labeled with various symbols. Panels F and G offer matched grayscale, microscopic, and imaging views of tissue sections with boundary markings and annotated features. Panels H display magnified histological images showing differences in tissue and cellular characteristics among annotated regions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a forest plot listing clinical and ultrasound characteristics affecting risk of peripheral margin positivity, including delineation method, age, primary site, tumor diameter, ultrasound morphology, and deep fascia abutment, with associated adjusted incidence rate ratios \(aIRR\). Panels B, C, and D present bar graphs comparing peripheral margin positivity percentages by delineation method \(HFUS-only 17.4 percent vs. HFUS+CEUS 5.1 percent\), ultrasound morphology \(ill-defined 16.6 percent vs. well-defined 4.4 percent\), and deep fascia abutment \(positive 17.7 percent vs. negative 3.6 percent\), with corresponding p-values indicating statistical significance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Forest plot summarizing multiple analyses comparing HFUS-only to HFUS plus CEUS, showing adjusted incidence rate ratios \(aIRRs\) with confidence intervals, all favoring reduced risk with combined imaging. Each analysis is listed with patient numbers, aIRR, confidence interval, and corresponding blue diamond and line for visual comparison against the null value of one.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a forest plot with stratified IRR and 95% confidence intervals for low, intermediate, and high risk groups, showing decreasing IRR from low to high risk and a P for interaction of 0.077. Panels B, C, and D display bar charts of peripheral margin positivity percentages for HFUS-only versus HFUS+CEUS within low, intermediate, and high risk groups, respectively, indicating a significant reduction in positivity for high risk \(P = 0.008\) when using HFUS+CEUS.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
